  "seed_note": "HYDROGEN_PEROXIDE -> PO appears in both section 4.1 and section 4.2 of the V1.1 document under route PO-HPPO; stored once. HR polyol, graft polyol and POP added 17 September 2026 on Stefan's instruction. POP is the same material as graft polyol and is carried as an alias of it, not as a second series. PHD and PIPA polyol added 18 September 2026: four polymer polyol chemistries appear in FNAG's own purchase history - SAN graft, SAN 10, PHD and PIPA - and PHD trades about 500 EUR/MT above the SAN grafts, so they are not one series. Fatty acid ester polyol and visco polyol added 18 September 2026: a different product is a different series, and Priplast 3186 trades at twice Ester 60 while the visco grades run 500 EUR/MT above conventional polyether. | 19 September 2026: per-step mass coefficients added to the isocyanate and polyol backbone. Each is derived from molar masses and carries its own derivation in mass_basis, so any of them can be rechecked without trusting this file. They are PER STEP: multiplied along a route they reproduce the route-level figures circulated on 19 September - toluene to TDI 0.5291 against 0.53, benzene to monomeric MDI 0.6243 against 0.62. Writing a route-level figure onto a single edge would double count.",
